prompt_b_reference_first:
Compare the two ultrasound reports for facts. Treat the reference as the only source of truth and ignore differences in phrasing, order, and style. Do not decide whether either statement is medically plausible. Find facts the candidate changes, adds without support, or leaves out. Mark changes to lesion presence, side, numeric measurements, category, diagnosis, or management-relevant facts as major; mark other factual changes as minor. If evidence is ambiguous, use unsure. These are provisional categories.
Each issue must include verbatim contiguous evidence: candidate_quote copied from the candidate and reference_quote copied from the reference. For a missing fact, use an empty candidate_quote and quote the missing fact in reference_quote. For an added unsupported fact, use an empty reference_quote. If no issue exists, return verdict clean and an empty issues list.
REFERENCE REPORT:
{ref}

CANDIDATE REPORT:
{cand}

Output one JSON object only with this schema: {"verdict":"clean|major|minor|unsure","issues":[{"candidate_quote":"...","reference_quote":"...","type":"contradicted|unsupported|omitted","severity":"major|minor|unsure","reason":"brief"}]}
